3.2 Job traces (400 words): PM100 (Marconi100, primary, CC-BY-4.0), F-DATA (Fugaku, five months, CC-BY-4.0), KIT FH2 (Parallel Workloads Archive; no power, 1 kW per job so energy weight is proportional to runtime; every SWF status is COMPLETED so TIMEOUT cannot be identified; licence terms to be checked, open item 8); job filter (COMPLETED, runtime at least 1 min, requested walltime at most 72 h and above 0); power treated as whole-job mean, never multiplied by nodes; walltime semantics audit (PM100 TIMEOUT jobs sit within 2 % of the limit; median actual-to-requested ratios by trace); NLR Kestrel not obtained (HTTP 503; open item 29), stated plainly. Fig 3 (ECDF of actual over requested runtime per trace, inset job-length classes). ref: antici2023pm100, antici2024fdata, feitelson2014pwa, klusacek2024.
3.3 Periods and what-if pairing (200 words): TRAIN 2018-07-01 to 2024-06-30, DEV 2024-07-01 to 2025-06-30, TEST 2025-07-01 to 2026-06-30, scored once after the freeze; arrivals fall between 2025-07-07 and 2026-06-14 (DEV row 4); jobs from 2016, 2020 and 2021 to 2023 are replayed on 2025-26 US grids at their local weekday and clock time (the what-if wording of L6.11; T4). Fig 2 (the 42 BAs: median daily intensity range against mean intensity, size = generation, colour = solar share).
