### 6 Discussion (1,550 words; W26, W27, L4)
6.1 What the 2 x 2 shows (300 words): the walltime-only cost is the oracle|req cell, parallel to the forecast-only gap of 101470; the runtime term versus forecast term by trace; the forecast term grows with slack; the interaction is small. Wording per W25.
6.2 Implications (300 words, counterfactual "would", "could"): operators (log requested and actual runtime, add a history-based predictor), users (walltime accuracy has a carbon value; a limit set too low kills the job, so the implication is for estimates, not shorter limits), scheduler designers (forecast and runtime are separate levers; no scheduler is ranked), signal providers (data latency, S2). Absolute effect reported beside the relative one (W18; key pending, open item 13). Never "will be realised".
6.3 Comparison with earlier work (250 words): why 12 h slack on a fixed grid gives smaller savings than the spatial or wind-driven studies, with no numeric comparison to their headline figures (W4); single-case 101407 headline against the pooled 42 BAs; 101216's zero-error effect has no analogue because the planner is one-stage; 101498's "runtimes could be estimated from previous runs" is the position the pred arm tests; code and data release mentioned once (101470, 101216, 101407, 100950 do not release).
6.4 Limitations and threats to validity (500 words; run-in bold labels, one weakness per paragraph with why the result may still hold and what would test it; W9, L4.3): Job sample and interval scope (T1; S1 exploratory beside); Data vintage and EIA publication delay (T2; S2); Average versus marginal signal, unverified oil, other and unknown factors, storage and imports excluded (T3, 4a, 4b; S3, X7 labelled); Cross-system pairing of foreign traces on US grids (T4; S6 text); No queueing, capacity, PUE or interruptibility (T5; X4 proxy); Estimand and BA selection on TEST availability (T6, M1); Delay-to-lowest-integral heuristic and a relative oracle (T7); KIT FH2 1 kW and status limits, frozen forecaster not tuned until S5, cleaned-hour counts and the TEST-year arrival gap (M2, M3, M7). Reference: sukprasert2024avgmarg, siler2012, hawkes2010, callaway2018, koebrich2025 for the marginal point.
6.5 Reproducibility (200 words): one-command rerun, frozen md5s, ledger, SHA256SUMS, Zenodo placeholder, private GitHub placeholder (R12, R13, W10).
Figures: none new. Tables: none new. Equations: none. Ledger keys: those of 5.2 to 5.5 re-quoted (identical values, W16).

### 7 Conclusion (300 words)
Results first (C1 to C3 with the keys of section 2), one sentence of implication (counterfactual), one sentence on limits, future work in one short paragraph (marginal signals, queue-aware simulation, a US trace such as NLR Kestrel when obtained, tuned forecasters if S5 does not close it). No new numbers.

