## 8. Open items (what waits on whom)

Owner decisions:
1. Title: approve option 1 or 2 of section 1 (or another LESSONS L8 option).
2. Author list and order, affiliations, emails, corresponding author (all `[USER]` placeholders in the text).
3. Figure count: 13 (merge FP 11 and 12) or 14 (G11).
4. Generative-AI declaration scope wording (progress.md open question 3); the section is written only after the owner confirms.
5. Funding sentence, competing-interest declaration (declarations-tool file), CRediT role assignment.
6. Graphical abstract: make one or not (R6; not established that it helps).
7. GitHub link (private until the owner gives it) and Zenodo DOI (owner uploads manually from the click-by-click guide); placeholders until then.

Reading and verification still to do:
8. KIT FH2 licence wording from the Parallel Workloads Archive page, before Data availability is written (G9).
9. A citation for the EIA-930 publication delay and a dataset reference for EIA-930 (G9; used in 3.1 and 6.4).
10. Read LACS (arXiv 2404.15211), COAST (arXiv 2609.05443) and LiteCast (arXiv 2511.06187) in full; fix their T1 cells, the gap sentence, the keys `lacs2024`, `coast2026`, `litecast2025` and the Related-work text (G10). Until then the three are named as "to read" and no claim about them goes beyond A13 and NOVELTY_SCAN.
11. Read Tsafrir 2007 (and Mu'alem and Feitelson 2001, Gaussier 2015, Fan and Lan 2017, Klusacek 2024) before any runtime-estimate inaccuracy figure is quoted (A15 s2).
12. Wiesner 2021, Sukprasert 2024 and Radovanovic 2023 runtime-handling cells in T1 are "not extracted" (G1r).

Ledger keys to add (by script, from files that exist):
13. Absolute-effect key: run-now mean intensity per trace in g CO2 per kWh of job energy, from the saved energy sums; needed in T4, 6.2 and E19 (G12, W24).
14. A ledger key for the median ratio of actual to requested runtime per trace (`tables/jobs_trace_stats.json` today).
15. Ledger keys for every Part B row (forecast MAE table, BA counts, trace row counts, TIMEOUT counts, flag shares, users after filter, arrival gap, bootstrap constants).
16. Post-hoc script for Shapley-term intervals on the saved bootstrap replicates (FF item 2); labelled exploratory if not in the frozen ledger; otherwise Fig 7 and T4 show point estimates only, with that stated.
17. Per-BA upper bounds of the within-BA interval for Fig 9 (FF item 3; same seed).

P4 and exploratory runs (all post-freeze; nothing has run as of 2026-11-12; A16 is implementing S4 and S2, queue runner pending):
18. S1 user-cluster uncertainty, S2 data latency (k = 1, 3, 6 h), S3 emission-factor sensitivity (two factor sets), S4 TIMEOUT-included (PM100), S5 tuned forecaster (Optuna, 100 trials, TRAIN only), settings fixed in P4_PLAN v2 (md5 `4eaf87c7e713c3ff967ff2b0b90e9cb9`). Cost order S4, S2, S5, S3, S1; resource gate at least 6 GB free RAM. Sections 5.9 and 6.4, Fig 14 and T6 hold placeholders until they run; if one does not finish, the text states "not run" and its limitation stays (W9).
19. X1 runtime-estimate sweep, X2 injected noise against the real forecast, X3 forecast-lead cap, X4 load concentration, X5 penalty concentration, X6 timing of the saving, X7 fossil-only marginal proxy (P4_PLAN_X, md5 `e2435f781d38cfe3aedc894e3267b0bd`); order X1, X3, X2, X4, X5, X6, X7 (after S3). X8 is not run. Each adds one panel or one T6 row, not a new main figure.
20. TIMEOUT-included run (PREREG s7.6, DEV row 2): part of S4; if it does not run, the paper reports PREREG item 6 as not run.

Figures and tables:
21. Figures 2 to 5 waiting for RAM (ci_clean, jobs, forecasts); fixes to Figures 1, 6 to 9, 13 and 14 (section 6); every caption at most 35 words; controller views each figure at print size.
22. Table script (`src/tables.py`, not yet written) for T2 to T6; DOCX with visible ruled tables.

Consistency and scope flags for the panel and the controller:
23. W25 and LESSONS L3.6 say "H1 to H3 are supported on all three traces"; PREREG s6 makes H1-H3 confirmatory on PM100 only, with F-DATA and KIT FH2 secondary (s7.6). This SPEC follows PREREG: the other traces' Holm p are reported as a secondary replication of the same test. The brief wording should be corrected.
24. A15 recommends 60 references; with LACS, COAST, LiteCast and about 5 missing items (LightGBM, Holm correction, GHG Protocol Scope 2, Electricity Maps, EIA-930 dataset; all to be harvested and Crossref-verified) the list reaches about 68 against the brief's target of 40 to 55 (R9). The panel or controller prunes about 13 (the 17 reserve entries are not counted).
25. Algorithm boxes: 5 against a topic-close range of 0 to 3 (F11); the owner rule asks for several. The panel decides whether Algorithms 1 and 2 merge.
26. Reproducibility gap: package versions and the exact commands of `analyze.py --boot twostage` and the near-limit run are not recorded (A08 s5); fix before 6.5 is written.
27. NLR Kestrel was not obtained (HTTP 503 on 2026-11-11; A07 user step 1); no US-site trace and no trace from the EIA-930 years. If it arrives before submission, add it as a secondary trace and redo 3.2 and T1; otherwise state its absence plainly in 3.2 and 6.4.
28. Highlights: no exemplar text in the 16 papers (G5); the five drafts in section 4 follow the Elsevier limits only.
29. Word-count basis: SPEC budgets about 11,500 words including captions against R2's 9,000 to 11,000; the Word render decides which section is cut (Discussion and Related work first).
30. Dates in the text: the pre-registration freeze is 2026-11-11 IST and the md5 in `research/PREREG.md5` was checked equal to `cfe984017ef7c790d851bfa2f519fde3` on 2026-11-12; the P4 plan md5 files also match their files.

## 9. Checks run by A18 on this SPEC

- Ledger values copied by script (`reg.py` in the session scratchpad), none typed. PM100 identity checks from stored values: `shapley.forecast` + `shapley.runtime` equals `shapley.gap` (0.01555 + 0.02303 = 0.03858); `H4_interaction.est` equals `shapley.interaction`; `p_holm` equals 3 x `p` at the floor 1/2001; E11 and E12 reproduce the stored terms from the four cell savings.
- E15 checked against `src/analyze.py` (null-centred on the estimate). PREREG, P4_PLAN and P4_PLAN_X md5 values checked.
- Wording rules applied: no "first", "novel", "to the best of our knowledge"; no claim about water, land use, spatial shifting or wind; no numeric comparison with the headline figures of other papers; "runtime term exceeds the forecast term" stated only for PM100 and KIT FH2.
- No em or en dashes in this file (scripted count 0 before the register was appended; the register contains only ASCII).
- Not done: no manuscript prose beyond plans and DRAFT lines; LACS, COAST, LiteCast, Tsafrir 2007 and the licence pages were not read (open items 8 to 11); figures were not re-viewed.
